# Locale packs are hashed BYTE FOR BYTE and served content-addressed: the
# wallet pins a SHA-256 per pack in its bundle and refuses anything else.
#
# On a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true, git writes these files with
# CRLF, so `npm run i18n:manifest` produces digests no other machine can
# reproduce. The manifest then looks fine locally, the commit stores LF, and
# every pack fails verification for every user — silently, because a rejected
# pack just leaves the wallet on English. Observed 2026-08-25; the deploy
# workflow's served-digest check caught it before it shipped.
#
# Pinning eol=lf makes the working tree, the object store and CI agree.
wallet/src/i18n/locales/*.json text eol=lf
wallet/src/i18n/manifest.ts    text eol=lf
